{"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/functionalgraphs\/functionalgraph"]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph of a function f on the vertices "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<n"},{"type":"text","text":": every vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" has exactly one out-edge,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v → f(v)"},{"type":"text","text":", and a fixed point is a self-loop. Also called a successor graph (Laaksonen,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Competitive Programmer’s Handbook","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":", §16.3)."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph"},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/CycleDecomposition"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/init(successors:)","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/init(vertexCount:successor:)"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/cycleDecomposition()","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/successor(of:)","doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/successor(of:steps:)"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\