m","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mapping statistics”, EUROCRYPT ’89). ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cycleDecomposition()"},{"text":" finds every cycle and tree in O(n);","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successor(of:steps:)"},{"text":" answers f^k(v) for any k.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For f given as a closure over a state space too large to store, use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"floydCycleDetection"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"brentCycleDetection"},{"text":", which need only ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"text":" states and O(1) memory.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" One ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" per vertex, ","type":"text"},{"code":"f(v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The edge leaving ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has position ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"positions and edge indices are both the source. For ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" vertex labels, use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"LabeledGraph<Label, FunctionalGraph>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"LabeledGraph(FunctionalGraph(g)!, labels: g.vertices)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gives a graph ","type":"text"},{"code":"g","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" its labels back.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph is immutable: build a new one to change f."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"title":"FunctionalGraph","externalID":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV","symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"